🐛 Describe the bug
When running tests with qtensor, it has the following errors:
RuntimeError: 0 INTERNAL ASSERT FAILED at "/pytorch/aten/src/ATen/quantized/Quantizer.cpp":125, please report a bug to PyTorch. unrecognized device for new_qtensor: xpu:0

This is because the XPU is not registered in qtensor.



      pytorch/aten/src/ATen/quantized/Quantizer.cpp


        Lines 116 to 126
      in
      d9d7cca







           if (device.is_cuda()) { 




             allocator = at::detail::getCUDAHooks().getCUDADeviceAllocator(); 




           } else if (device.is_cpu()) { 




             allocator = at::getCPUAllocator(); 




           } else if (device.is_meta()) { 




             allocator = GetAllocator(kMeta); 




           } else if (device.is_privateuseone()) { 




             allocator = GetAllocator(kPrivateUse1); 




           } else { 




             TORCH_INTERNAL_ASSERT(0, "unrecognized device for new_qtensor: ", device); 




           } 





A PR is needed to add xpu support to it.
Versions
PyTorch 2.6 release.
